# Environment for the ATLAS market-hours service.
#
#   sudo cp deploy/atlas.env.example /etc/atlas.env
#   sudo chown root:root /etc/atlas.env && sudo chmod 600 /etc/atlas.env
#   # fill in the values, then: sudo systemctl restart atlas-market-hours
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Every secret in this repo is read from the environment (atlas/config.py is
# os.environ.get for all of them), and until now the environment came from the
# crontab header. systemd does not read a crontab, so under the service every
# one of these is unset unless it is here.
#
# The first symptom was quiet rather than loud: "Telegram not configured —
# skipping message". telegram.send() logs that and returns, so nothing fails,
# and a service that alerts on every failure would have alerted into a void for
# a whole session. market_open.preflight() now refuses to start without the
# alert channel for that reason.
#
# LIVE TRADING — CORRECTING WHAT THIS FILE USED TO SAY
#
# An earlier version of this comment claimed live trading "is in code and not
# in the environment, so turning it on is a commit and not an ssh session".
# That was wrong. config.LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED has always read ATLAS_LIVE from
# the environment.
#
# It is now decided by GO_LIVE_DATE in atlas/config.py -- shadow through
# 2026-09-17, live from 2026-09-18 -- with ATLAS_LIVE as an override in either
# direction:
#
#   ATLAS_LIVE=false   forces SHADOW whatever the date. The emergency brake:
#                      set it here, restart, and no real order can be placed.
#                      Needs no commit and no deploy.
#   ATLAS_LIVE=true    forces LIVE before the date, for a deliberate test.
#   unset (default)    the date decides.
#
# Leave it unset unless you mean one of those. It is listed below commented out
# so that setting it is a visible act rather than a remembered one.
# ATLAS_LIVE=false

# ── required: the service refuses to start without these ──────────
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── required once trading is live; also read in shadow, because the ──
# ── funds and position gates query the broker either way ────────────
ZERODHA_API_KEY=
ZERODHA_API_SECRET=
ZERODHA_USER_ID=
ZERODHA_PASSWORD=
ZERODHA_TOTP_SECRET=

# ── not needed by this service ────────────────────────────────────
# The loop reads prices with the Upstox token FILE
# (data/upstox_token.json), not these. They belong to the login job that
# refreshes that file, which stays on cron.
# UPSTOX_API_KEY=
# UPSTOX_API_SECRET=
# UPSTOX_MOBILE=
# UPSTOX_PIN=
# UPSTOX_TOTP_SECRET=

# Optional override; the default is the project URL in atlas/config.py.
# SUPABASE_URL=
